Turn 2 of 4 — model check. Still no program JSON.

Before extracting anything, restate the target data model in your own words, in five or six sentences:

- a **track** is one sequential line of work; steps in the same track never overlap, and anything that happens while something else happens belongs in a different track;
- a **step** has exactly one duration kind: `fixed` (`seconds`), `variable` (`minSeconds`, `maxSeconds`, `defaultSeconds`) or `indefinite` (runs until the person ends it);
- a **startTrigger** ties a step to the clock or to another step — `programStart`, `programStartOffset`, `afterStep`, `afterStepWithBuffer`, `manual`, `onAbort`, `compound`;
- `stepId`s are unique across the WHOLE program, not per track;
- every `task` a step occupies needs a matching `resourceConstraints` entry, and that entry's `maxConcurrent` is what stops two steps sharing one oven, one thermocycler or one PA;
- work repeated n times (n trays, n samples, n aircraft) is `replicates: {count: n, mode: "serial" | "parallel" | "stagger"}` on ONE step — never n hand-copied steps or tracks. Chain what follows each repetition with `{"type":"afterStep","stepId":"<step>","instances":"each"}`, give the step that waits for all of them `{"instances":"all"}`, and when the holding area between them only fits k at a time (a rack that holds two trays, a rotor that holds six tubes, a taxiway that holds two aircraft) set `replicates.maxInFlight: k` so the upstream step is held back instead of stranding the downstream one.

`rhylthyme://guide/authoring` is the full cheat-sheet, and `rhylthyme://schema/program` the schema, if you want to check a rule.

Then list the resource constraints you expect this protocol to need — one `task` per line with the `maxConcurrent` you intend to declare and how many people are working — and end with that list as JSON in a single ```json fenced block:

```json
{
  "acknowledgement": "tracks are sequential lines of work; one duration kind per step; triggers link steps; every task needs a resourceConstraint; stepIds are global",
  "resourceConstraints": [
    { "task": "oven", "maxConcurrent": 1 },
    { "task": "burner", "maxConcurrent": 2 },
    { "task": "prep", "maxConcurrent": 2 }
  ],
  "actors": 2
}
```

completion.text:
A track is one sequential line of work, so steps on that track do not overlap; simultaneous work must be placed on separate tracks. Each step has exactly one duration kind: fixed, variable, or indefinite, with the fields required by that kind. A start trigger connects a step to the program clock, an offset, another step, a manual action, an abort, or a compound condition. Every step ID must be unique across the entire program, and every task used by a step must have a matching resource constraint whose `maxConcurrent` limits simultaneous use. Repeated work is represented once with `replicates`, while `"each"` chains per-instance follow-up work, `"all"` creates a barrier, and `maxInFlight` limits how many repeated items can occupy a holding area. This protocol has one operator, so operator-occupied work is limited to one person, while each listed instrument is also limited to its single available unit.

Expected resource constraints:

- `operator` — `maxConcurrent: 1`; one person is working.
- `thermocycler` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.
- `microcentrifuge` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.
- `microwave` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.
- `gelRig` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.
- `transilluminator` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.
- `coldBlock` — `maxConcurrent: 1`.

```json
{
  "acknowledgement": "Tracks are sequential lines of work; each step has one duration kind; start triggers connect steps to the clock or dependencies; stepIds are unique across the whole program; every task needs a matching resourceConstraint; repeated work uses replicates with each/all chaining and maxInFlight where a holding capacity applies.",
  "resourceConstraints": [
    {
      "task": "operator",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "thermocycler",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "microcentrifuge",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "microwave",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "gelRig",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "transilluminator",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    },
    {
      "task": "coldBlock",
      "maxConcurrent": 1
    }
  ],
  "actors": 1
}
```
